      "en": "JavaScript runs one line at a time (one thread). If it waited two seconds for an API reply **synchronously**, the page would freeze and the server would answer nobody. The fix: **asynchronous** code — you ask for something, carry on, and when the reply arrives its code runs. That is what **non-blocking** means."
